        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "Throughout the book, boldface type has been used to highlight key terms at the point in a chapter where the main discussion occurs. Italic type is used to set off important terms with a lesser degree of emphasis. At the end of the book is an expanded glossary, covering all the major terms common to cell biology; it should be the first resort for a reader who encounters an unfamiliar technical word."
          }
